Governance policies should be reviewed periodically to ensure they continue supporting organisational objectives as cloud environments evolve.

A governance review typically examines:

* Policy effectiveness
* Role assignments
* Compliance status
* Cost management
* Security controls
* Documentation
* Resource organisation

# Real-Life Example:
For example, after acquiring another company, an enterprise may update governance policies to accommodate additional subscriptions and new business requirements.

# Real-Life Use Case:
A real-life use case is maintaining governance consistency during rapid organisational growth.

Regular governance reviews ensure cloud environments remain secure, compliant, and well managed.
